  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provsion of Lifesaving  Health and Nutrition response to displaced people and at risk of and famine in West Kordofan Al Odeya Locality</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltbrgtThe life-saving intervention proposes to reach 46,973&#xA0;people through 4 static integrated health and nutrition facilities and one mobile clinic services in Al Odeya locality, West Kordofan.&#xA0; ltbrgtHEALTH: The project will provide primary health care support for 34,581&#xA0;people in the 4 health facilities and one mobile clinic around the catchment of the facilities, provide life-saving pharma, preventative and curative services, incentivize SMOH health workers, set up minimum hygiene requirements for treatment, and conduct one training on preparedness and ER health response.&#xA0; ltbrgtNUTRITION: Nutrition activities will be integrated in the health care support within the same facilities benefiting 13,400 individuals. The intervention will run 4 OTP (Outpatient Therapeutic Programme), one Stabilization Center within one of the health centers in Al Odeya hospital and will also provide screening and nutrition support while running the clinics/outreach services. The nutrition services will follow CMAM protocol and will target 13,400 and their mothers with CMAM programme.&#xA0;&#xA0; ltbrgtFollowing SHF&apos;s strategy on localization, the intervention will work with AORD-a local NNGO and the partner will focus on mobilization and community engagement to reach more people with the integrated services.&#xA0; ltbrgtLooking at the current crisis causing access impediments, the intervention is regularly updating the conflict analysis and response document (Annexed herein) and plan for alternative ways to deliver services. The intervention will be implemented in RSF controlled areas with high probability of access limitations through the SAF controlled locations, therefore cross-border operation and logistics support from South Sudan is considered a possibility during the intervention.&#xA0; ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
